---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
import InstanceNote from "../components/api/InstanceNote.astro";
import OptionsTable from "../components/api/OptionsTable.astro";
import PropertiesTable from "../components/api/PropertiesTable.astro";
import { defineSections } from "../lib/sections";

const S = defineSections([
  { id: "anatomy", label: "Introduction", heading: false },
  { id: "initialization", label: "Initialization" },
  { id: "markup", label: "Markup" },
  { id: "options", label: "Options" },
  { id: "methods", label: "Methods" },
  { id: "properties", label: "Properties" },
  { id: "custom-html", label: "Custom HTML" },
  { id: "callback", label: "Callback" },
  { id: "styling", label: "Styling" },
  { id: "dismissal", label: "Dismissing snackbars", heading: "Dismiss a snackbar programmatically" },
]);
---
<DocsLayout page="snackbar" sections={S}>
<p>Snackbars with an action are persistent and dismissible by default. Escape dismisses a focused snackbar. Closing it restores focus only when focus is still inside the bar. If you set a finite timer, it still pauses during focus or hover.</p>

  <Section {...S.anatomy}>
        <p class="flow-text">
          Snackbars show short updates about app processes at the bottom
          of the screen. They should not interrupt browsing. People can
          keep using the page without interacting with the bar. Write the
          bar as a <code>.snackbar</code> with a <code>&lt;p&gt;</code> for
          the supporting text. A trailing <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> is
          the optional action, and a <code>.circle</code> button is the
          optional close.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tokens follow the
          <a href="https://m3.material.io/components/snackbar/specs">M3 snackbar spec</a>.
          The container is <code>inverse-surface</code> with 4dp corners,
          elevation 3, and a 48dp minimum height. Supporting text is
          <code>body-medium</code> in <code>inverse-on-surface</code>,
          up to two lines. The action is a <code>label-large</code> text button in
          <code>inverse-primary</code>. Close is a 24dp
          <code>inverse-on-surface</code> icon. On compact viewports the
          bar is inset 8dp from the edges. From the Medium breakpoint up it
          fits its content, between 344dp and 672dp wide, and sits centered 24dp from the bottom.
        </p>
        <p>
          A text-only snackbar stays for 4 seconds by default. Setting <code>action</code>
          changes the defaults to <code>displayLength: Infinity</code> and
          <code>dismissible: true</code>. Explicit options override these defaults. Only one
          snackbar shows at a time.
        </p>
        <p>
          Snackbar is not in <code>AutoInit()</code>. Construct one
          when you need it, or put a static <code>.snackbar</code> in
          the page and add <code>.active</code> to pin it.
        </p>

        <p>
          <button type="button" id="snackbar-basic">Show</button>
          <button type="button" class="tonal" id="snackbar-action">Show with action</button>
          <button type="button" class="outlined" id="snackbar-close">Show with close</button>
        </p>

        <div class="snackbar">
          <p>Photo saved to album</p>
        </div>
        <div class="snackbar">
          <p>Item archived</p>
          <button type="button">Undo</button>
        </div>
        <div class="snackbar">
          <p>Can't send photo. Retry in 5 seconds.</p>
          <button type="button">Retry</button>
          <button type="button" class="circle" aria-label="Dismiss">
            <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">close</span>
          </button>
        </div>
<Code code={`
new Expressive.Snackbar({ text: 'Photo saved to album' });

new Expressive.Snackbar({
  text: 'Item archived',
  action: 'Undo',
  onAction: function() { /* restore */ }
});

new Expressive.Snackbar({
  text: "Can't send photo. Retry in 5 seconds.",
  action: 'Retry',
  dismissible: true
});
`} />
        <p>
          The constructor wraps <code>text</code> in a
          <code>&lt;p&gt;</code> and appends the action and close when
          those options are set. The live region is
          <code>role="status"</code> with <code>aria-live="polite"</code>,
          so it announces without stealing focus.
        </p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.initialization}>
    <p>Actions and Dismiss use ordinary Tab navigation. When reaching the end of the page would be cumbersome, put a visible notification-actions button near the task trigger. Its click handler can call <code>instance.el.querySelector('button, a[href]')?.focus()</code>. Do not call it automatically when showing a snackbar.</p>
    <p>The snackbar handles Escape only inside itself. Escape there does not also dismiss an enclosing dialog. If an action moves focus elsewhere, closing leaves focus there. For timed feedback, keep an equivalent persistent message.</p>
        <p>
          The IIFE bundle exposes <code>Expressive.Snackbar</code>. Snackbar is
          not in <code>AutoInit()</code>, so construct one when you need it.
        </p>
<Code code={`
new Expressive.Snackbar({
  text: 'I am a snackbar!'
});
`} />
        <p>One way to hook that up is a click handler on a button:</p>
<Code code={`
<button type="button" id="snackbar-basic">Show</button>
`} />
<Code code={`
document.getElementById('snackbar-basic').addEventListener('click', function() {
  new Expressive.Snackbar({ text: 'I am a snackbar!' });
});
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.markup}>
        <p>
          The same anatomy works as static HTML. Without
          <code>.active</code> the bar stays in the document flow, which is useful for previews.
          With <code>.active</code> it pins to the bottom of the
          viewport, centered from the Medium breakpoint. Add
          <code>.top</code> only if you must move it off the bottom.
        </p>
        <p>
          <button type="button" class="tonal" id="snackbar-static">Show static snackbar</button>
        </p>
        <div class="snackbar" id="static-snackbar">
          <p>Single-line snackbar with action</p>
          <button type="button">Action</button>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="snackbar">
  <p>Photo saved to album</p>
</div>

<div class="snackbar">
  <p>Item archived</p>
  <button type="button">Undo</button>
</div>

<div class="snackbar active">
  <p>Single-line snackbar with action</p>
  <button type="button">Action</button>
</div>
`} />
        <p>
          A bar with <code>.active</code> does not dismiss itself. Add and remove the
          class, or use the constructor if you want the 4-second timer and
          swipe-to-dismiss.
        </p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.options}>
        <p>You can customize each snackbar with these options.</p>
        <OptionsTable>            <tr>
              <td><code>text</code></td>
              <td>String</td>
              <td><code>''</code></td>
              <td>Plain-text supporting text, wrapped in a <code>&lt;p&gt;</code>. If set, it replaces any HTML from <code>snackbarId</code>.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>action</code></td>
              <td>String</td>
              <td><code>''</code></td>
              <td>Optional action label, shown as a trailing text button.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>onAction</code></td>
              <td>Function</td>
              <td><code>null</code></td>
              <td>Called when the action button is pressed. The snackbar still dismisses.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>dismissible</code></td>
              <td>Boolean</td>
              <td><code>false</code></td>
              <td>Show a trailing close icon button. Defaults to true when <code>action</code> is set or <code>displayLength</code> is <code>Infinity</code>, so a swipe is never the only way to dismiss. An explicit false still applies.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>snackbarId</code></td>
              <td>String</td>
              <td>—</td>
              <td>Id of a <code>&lt;template&gt;</code> (or another element) used as the snackbar body. The snackbar clones a template. It moves any other element inside itself and puts it back on dismissal or replacement, so you can reuse the same ID.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>displayLength</code></td>
              <td>Number</td>
              <td><code>4000</code></td>
              <td>How long the snackbar stays before it dismisses, in milliseconds. Default 4s without an action, or <code>Infinity</code> with an action. If you set a finite timeout, give equivalent persistent feedback elsewhere in the application.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>inDuration</code></td>
              <td>Number</td>
              <td><code>300</code></td>
              <td>Enter transition duration, in milliseconds.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>outDuration</code></td>
              <td>Number</td>
              <td><code>375</code></td>
              <td>Exit transition duration, in milliseconds.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>classes</code></td>
              <td>String</td>
              <td><code>''</code></td>
              <td>Space-separated classes added to the snackbar. <code>rounded</code> is a stadium. <code>top</code> moves the bar off the bottom.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>completeCallback</code></td>
              <td>Function</td>
              <td><code>null</code></td>
              <td>Called when the snackbar is dismissed.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>activationPercent</code></td>
              <td>Number</td>
              <td><code>0.8</code></td>
              <td>Fraction of the snackbar's width a drag must travel to dismiss it.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>root</code></td>
              <td>Element</td>
              <td><code>null</code></td>
              <td>
                Any element in the tree the snackbar should render into. Pass one
                when the page lives in a shadow root, so the snackbar appends its
                container there instead of to <code>document.body</code>.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>replace</code></td>
              <td>Boolean</td>
              <td><code>false</code></td>
              <td>
                Show at once, cutting the snackbar on screen short, instead of waiting
                behind it. Copy buttons use this so a second copy answers right away.
              </td>
            </tr>
  </OptionsTable>
        <p>
          One snackbar shows at a time. A new one waits until the one on screen is
          dismissed, then shows, so updates appear in order. A queued snackbar
          captures focus and fires <code>expressive:open</code> when it appears.
          If you dismiss it while it is still waiting, it runs
          <code>completeCallback</code> and never shows. A snackbar built from
          <code>snackbarId</code> takes its element when it shows, so its
          <code>el</code> is unset while it waits.
        </p>  </Section>
  <Section {...S.methods}>
        <InstanceNote plugin="Snackbar" lead="Instance methods are called on the snackbar. You can get the instance like this:" />

        <h5 class="light">.dismiss();</h5>
        <p>Dismiss this snackbar with its exit animation. Runs <code>completeCallback</code> when the animation finishes.</p>
<Code code={`
instance.dismiss();
`} />

        <h5 class="light">Snackbar.dismissAll();</h5>
        <p>Dismiss the snackbar on screen and every one waiting behind it.</p>
<Code code={`
Expressive.Snackbar.dismissAll();
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.properties}>
        <PropertiesTable el={"The snackbar element."}>            <tr>
              <td><code>panning</code></td>
              <td>Boolean</td>
              <td>Whether the snackbar is being dragged.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>timeRemaining</code></td>
              <td>Number</td>
              <td>Milliseconds left before the snackbar dismisses.</td>
            </tr>
  </PropertiesTable>  </Section>
  <Section {...S["custom-html"]}>
        <p>
          Pass <code>snackbarId</code> pointing at a
          <code>&lt;template&gt;</code>. The snackbar clones the template's
          first child. Leave <code>text</code> empty to keep the HTML. Use the
          same anatomy as a static snackbar. For custom links or controls, set <code>displayLength: Infinity</code> explicitly and add a close control with <code>dismissible: true</code>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <button type="button" class="tonal mr-3 mb-3" id="snackbar-html-1">Show Snackbar 1</button>
          <button type="button" class="tonal mb-3" id="snackbar-html-2">Show Snackbar 2</button>
        </p>
        <template id="my-snackbar-1">
          <div>
            <p>This is snackbar nº1 with a <a href="https://github.com">link</a></p>
          </div>
        </template>
        <template id="my-snackbar-2">
          <div>
            <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">insert_chart</span>
            <p>This is snackbar nº2</p>
          </div>
        </template>
<Code code={`
<button type="button" class="tonal" id="snackbar-html-1">Show Snackbar 1</button>
<template id="my-snackbar-1">
  <div>
    <p>This is snackbar nº1 with a <a href="https://github.com">link</a></p>
  </div>
</template>
`} />
<Code code={`
new Expressive.Snackbar({ snackbarId: 'my-snackbar-1', displayLength: Infinity, dismissible: true });
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.callback}>
        <p>Run a function when the snackbar is dismissed.</p>
        <p>
          <button type="button" id="snackbar-callback">Show Snackbar</button>
        </p>
<Code code={`
new Expressive.Snackbar({
  text: 'I will call back when dismissed',
  completeCallback: function() {
    new Expressive.Snackbar({ text: 'Your snackbar was dismissed' });
  }
});
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.styling}>
        <p>
          Pass classes in the <code>classes</code> option.
          <code>rounded</code> is a 24dp stadium. The M3 default is 4dp corners.
          Snackbars sit at the bottom unless you add <code>top</code>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <button type="button" id="snackbar-rounded">Show round Snackbar</button>
          <button type="button" class="tonal" id="snackbar-top">Show at top</button>
        </p>
<Code code={`
new Expressive.Snackbar({
  text: 'I am a snackbar!',
  classes: 'rounded'
});

new Expressive.Snackbar({
  text: 'Posted from the top',
  classes: 'top'
});
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.dismissal}>
        <p>
          To remove a specific snackbar, get the instance from the snackbar
          element and call <code>dismiss()</code>. Dragging it past 80% of its width,
          or flicking it, also dismisses it. After a short drag, pausing for at
          least 100ms before release lets the snackbar snap back. Cancelling a swipe leaves the snackbar
          open and does not affect the next gesture. The action and close
          buttons are not swipe handles.
        </p>
        <p>
          <button type="button" class="mr-3 mb-3" id="snackbar-dismiss-show">Show Snackbar</button>
          <button type="button" class="tonal mr-3 mb-3" id="snackbar-dismiss-one">Dismiss a snackbar</button>
          <button type="button" class="tonal mb-3" id="snackbar-dismiss-all">Dismiss all</button>
        </p>
<Code code={`
const snackbarElement = document.querySelector('#snackbar-container .snackbar');
Expressive.Snackbar.getInstance(snackbarElement)?.dismiss();
`} />
        <h5 class="light">Dismiss all snackbars</h5>
<Code code={`
Expressive.Snackbar.dismissAll();
`} />
  </Section>
</DocsLayout>
